<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xri version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.pixinsight.com/xri" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
     xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.pixinsight.com/xri http://pixinsight.com/xri/xri-1.0.xsd">
   <description>
      <p>CabraSpace PixInsight repository — astrophysics scripts that put the stars of your own images in context (distances, 3D, stellar chemistry). Each script is a separate package: install only the ones you want.</p>
      <p>Copyright &#169; 2026 CabraSpace.</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.6:1.9.99">
      <package fileName="20261105-FieldDepth3D-1.0.1.zip" sha1="5e266f8e02ec20a361986f27fde2587224ced1ef" type="script" releaseDate="20261105">
         <title>FieldDepth3D 1.0.1 — distances and 3D view of your image</title>
         <remove>
            src/scripts/CabraSpace/FieldDepth3D
            doc/scripts/FieldDepth3D
            doc/scripts/FieldDepth3D_es
            rsc/icons/script/FieldDepth3D
         </remove>
         <description>
            <p>FieldDepth3D places every star, cluster, nebula and galaxy of a plate-solved image at its real distance and shows the field in 3D: fly-throughs, a time machine for stellar motions, the Galaxy in 3D and video export (AVI; MP4 only with an ffmpeg the user chooses).</p>
            <p>Menu: Script &gt; CabraSpace &gt; FieldDepth3D. Requires an astrometric solution (ImageSolver).</p>
            <p>Network: it queries public astronomical catalogues (Gaia DR3, VizieR, SIMBAD, Zenodo) over HTTPS with the image coordinates only; no image data is ever uploaded. Downloads are validated and cached, sealed with SHA-256, outside the PixInsight installation. Full details in the script documentation (button ?).</p>
            <p>Copyright &#169; 2026 CabraSpace.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
      <package fileName="20261105-StellarChemistry-0.3.1.zip" sha1="cacb5fdba277440a334b1b6121fe9eae8d210a66" type="script" releaseDate="20261105">
         <title>StellarChemistry 0.3.1 — chemical archaeology of the stars in your image</title>
         <remove>
            src/scripts/CabraSpace/StellarChemistry
            doc/scripts/StellarChemistry
            doc/scripts/StellarChemistry_es
            rsc/icons/script/StellarChemistry
         </remove>
         <description>
            <p>StellarChemistry reads the stars of a plate-solved image against Gaia DR3 and the APOGEE, GALAH and LAMOST surveys: metallicity, alpha elements, ages, Galactic population, orbits and chemical families, explained in plain language.</p>
            <p>Menu: Script &gt; CabraSpace &gt; StellarChemistry. Requires an astrometric solution (ImageSolver).</p>
            <p>Network: it queries public astronomical catalogues (VizieR TAP and its mirrors, SIMBAD) over HTTPS with the image coordinates only; no image data is ever uploaded. Responses are validated and cached, sealed with SHA-256, outside the PixInsight installation. Full details in the script documentation (button ?).</p>
            <p>Copyright &#169; 2026 CabraSpace.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
